From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 07:23:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] sc-compose checkpoint 2: the simulators, the output
 clause and the statistical switch (hbcSecure_compose steps 1-2)

The simulator S_A (S_B) post-processes the hybrid simulator by Phi: L(n) runs of rho's
simulator on the recomputed call inputs, the answer blocks and coin blocks, assembled into a view
of the composed protocol (Sim.lean: exists_simulator; Assembly.lean: asmView). The output clause
of HBCSecure rho G with the worst-case inputs as advice makes each run correct except with
negligible probability (Correct.lean: exists_correct, uprob_not_goodRuns_le). Under GoodRuns the
real samples are the assembled views of the real run views with the hybrid main phase
(Runs.lean: realA_compose_eq, realB_compose_eq), and the statistical switch bounds the rest
(Probability.lean: distAdv_le_uprob_of_eq). hbcSecure_compose keeps its sorry.
